/-!
# A checked star-pair comparison for census representative 4

The native conjugator carries the representative to the second marked
involution. The conjugate of the first marked involution acts on one specified
kernel pair by the displayed mask. This is a matrix identity in the faithful
native representation, to be consumed by the full residual character.
Source: Kleidman--Wilson (1988), p.487, Corollary 1.1.4. The imported ATLAS
matrix and word attribution is retained in LocalInvolutionCensus/Fusion/source/README.md.
-/

